{"id":"6da127fa38ab1838","group":"27","path":"27/27-ex-thresholddummy.md","title":"A nonzero weight can belong to an inessential variable","display":"ex-thresholddummy — A nonzero weight can belong to an inessential variable","type":"example","metadata":{"type":"example","book":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications","book_abbrev":"27","label":"27-ex-thresholddummy","aliases":["27-ex-thresholddummy"],"display":"ex-thresholddummy — A nonzero weight can belong to an inessential variable","depends_on":["[[27-df-threshold]]"],"source_file":"C:/Users/lzy/Documents/BaiduSyncdisk/calibre/Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer/Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)/Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf","source_section":"§9.2 Example 9.4","source_printed_pages":"410","source_pdf_pages":"434","verification_status":"source-example-and-all-inputs-checked"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"example"},{"key":"book","html":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"27"},{"key":"label","html":"27-ex-thresholddummy"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>27-ex-thresholddummy</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"ex-thresholddummy — A nonzero weight can belong to an inessential variable"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"d0db491e5f6359f5\" href=\"?note=d0db491e5f6359f5\" title=\"27-df-threshold\">27-df-threshold</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_file","html":"C:/Users/lzy/Documents/BaiduSyncdisk/calibre/Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer/Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)/Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf"},{"key":"source_section","html":"§9.2 Example 9.4"},{"key":"source_printed_pages","html":"410"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"434"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-example-and-all-inputs-checked"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f:\\mathbb B^4\\to\\mathbb B\">\\(f:\\mathbb B^4\\to\\mathbb B\\)</span> 由 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f(x,y,z,u)=(x\\wedge y)\\vee z\">\\(f(x,y,z,u)=(x\\wedge y)\\vee z\\)</span> 定义，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}\">\\(\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}\\)</span>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Sep}\">\\(\\mathrm{Sep}\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"d0db491e5f6359f5\" href=\"?note=d0db491e5f6359f5\" title=\"27-df-threshold\">27-df-threshold</a>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"((2,4,6,1),5)\\in\\mathrm{Sep}(f).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[((2,4,6,1),5)\\in\\mathrm{Sep}(f).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\forall(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb B^3\\;(f(x,y,z,0)=f(x,y,z,1)),\\qquad1\\ne0.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\forall(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb B^3\\;(f(x,y,z,0)=f(x,y,z,1)),\\qquad1\\ne0.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>原书 Example 9.4，印刷 p.410／PDF p.434。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"z=1\">\\(z=1\\)</span> 或 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x=y=1\">\\(x=y=1\\)</span> 时得分至少6，其余情况至多5。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"u\">\\(u\\)</span> 从未影响输出，是“非零权蕴含本质变量”的直接反例；已穷举16输入核对。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"27-df-threshold","status":"resolved","id":"d0db491e5f6359f5","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-threshold]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-threshold","status":"resolved","id":"d0db491e5f6359f5","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$f:\\mathbb B^4\\to\\mathbb B$ 由 $f(x,y,z,u)=(x\\wedge y)\\vee z$ 定义，$\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}$；$\\mathrm{Sep}$ 见 [[27-df-threshold]]。","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"f:\\mathbb B^4\\to\\mathbb B","display":false},{"tex":"f(x,y,z,u)=(x\\wedge y)\\vee z","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Sep}","display":false},{"tex":"((2,4,6,1),5)\\in\\mathrm{Sep}(f).","display":true},{"tex":"\\forall(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb B^3\\;(f(x,y,z,0)=f(x,y,z,1)),\\qquad1\\ne0.","display":true},{"tex":"z=1","display":false},{"tex":"x=y=1","display":false},{"tex":"u","display":false}],"bytes":1225,"backlinks":[{"id":"5244dbb38da17b8a","anchor":"ref-83","locations":["正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"[[27-ex-thresholddummy|ex-thresholddummy — A nonzero weight can belong to an inessential variable]]"}],"outgoing":["d0db491e5f6359f5"]}